WEBVTT

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.580
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.710
The Pokémon World Championships...

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.170
A trial to crown
the greatest Pokémon battler.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.390
In the hopes of battling Dande,
the current Supreme Monarch,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.560
Satoshi is participating
in the Championships.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:44.020
All right, it’s time for...

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.530
Pokémon Battles!

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.530
Pokémon Catching!

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.740
I’ll go on ahead
to Miare Gym, then!

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:52.370
Yeah! I’ll be right there
once I’ve caught something!

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.120
Right!

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:58.410
Satoshi has arranged to meet up
with Citron and Eureka,

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:01.540
with whom he once
traveled through Kalos.

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:02.830
Huh?

00:01:05.210 --> 00:01:08.720
The Pokémon World Championships,
Hyper Class!

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:14.470
Tomorrow’s battle is between one of the Kalos Elite Four,
Competitor Dracaena, currently ranked 12th!

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:15.470
And...

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:16.970
Wha— That’s me!

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:20.690
The New Star of Kanto,
who is quickly rising up the ranks,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.440
Competitor Satoshi,
currently ranked 15th!

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.320
So, Competitor Dracaena...
The day is nearly here.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.110
Satoshi is strong, isn’t he?
Quite, quite strong indeed!

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:33.950
It fills me with joy!

00:01:33.950 --> 00:01:37.660
Thank you for those words.
That was Competitor Dracaena!

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.710
Pikachu! If we can’t get past her,
we won’t have any hope of reaching Mr. Dande!

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.480
What is it?

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.160
A Keromatsu!

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.990
Monster Ball, go!

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.380
What is this stuff?!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:52.920
It’s Keromousse!

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:55.420
Keromousse?

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:58.760
Yeah!
A talent only Keromatsu has!

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:01.800
Huh...

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.970
All right! Keromatsu!

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.350
Let’s battle!

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.110
Wild Bolt!

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.240
Ahh!

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.500
Berobelt is unable to battle!

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.670
Rentorar wins!

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.290
As such, the winner is
Gym Leader Citron!

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.550
Citron!

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:37.510
Satoshi! Pikachu!
I’ve been waiting for you!

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.930
Your next opponent
came as quite a shock.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:46.600
A battle against Ms. Dracaena
of the Elite Four!

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.940
Yeah! My Pokémon are
really hyped up, too!

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.900
Then how about I join you,
like old times?

00:04:52.310 --> 00:04:53.900
Come on out,
everyone!

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:58.030
Ahh!

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.400
Kairyu?!

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:02.910
What’s that Pokémon?!

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.200
It’s called Uonoragon.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:09.160
It’s a rare Pokémon,
revived from fossils from Galar.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.170
Nice to meet you,
Uonoragon.

00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.000
Huh?

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:15.500
Horudo?!

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.510
Yes, my Horubee evolved!

00:05:22.010 --> 00:05:26.600
Horudo. Digging Pokémon.
Normal/Ground type.

00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:30.730
With power equal to an excavator, it can dig through dense bedrock.

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:40.700
I’ve never seen a Pokémon
like him before, either.

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.280
He’s Negigaknight.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:45.030
Galarian Kamonegi’s
evolved form.

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.620
Wow...

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:49.120
Hmm?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:49.540
Huh?

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:25.410
What?!

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:36.960
You can’t pull it out?

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.300
Come on...

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.300
Ahh!

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.190
That was a surprise...

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:59.270
That Uonoragon’s surprisingly quick,
considering its size.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.320
It’s never done that before!

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.650
Why did it suddenly go
for Negigaknight?

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:06.780
Who knows...?

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:11.790
Again?

00:07:35.940 --> 00:07:37.650
Uonoragon!

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:40.440
That almost looks like fishing...

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.990
Come on. Open your mouth,
Uonoragon.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:52.950
Whoa!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.880
Man...

00:08:00.500 --> 00:08:04.760
He might be on the verge of
pulling off a new move.

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:05.840
Huh?!

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:17.520
Monster Ball, go!

00:08:25.110 --> 00:08:28.740
Keromatsu’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:08:28.740 --> 00:08:30.910
I-I caught a Keromatsu!

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:31.820
Good job!

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:36.080
Keromatsu! Bubble Frog Pokémon!
Water type!

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.420
It protects itself by covering its body
in delicate bubbles!

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:43.000
Beneath its happy-go-lucky air, it keeps a watchful eye on its surroundings!

00:08:45.630 --> 00:08:48.170
That took a long time...

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:52.010
Let’s see, what way takes me
to Miare Gym...?

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:54.430
I was just going to the Gym!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.390
Really?

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:57.180
It’s my bro’s Gym!

00:08:57.180 --> 00:08:59.060
Oh...

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:00.850
Your <i>bro’s?!</i>

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:02.860
Yeah!

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:05.610
Hmm...

00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:11.200
That move was Star Assault.
A move that only Negigaknight can learn.

00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:12.910
Star Assault!

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:17.200
He hasn’t quite perfected it yet,
but that was still an impressive move!

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.910
I hope he can learn it somehow...

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.080
I wanna use it in my battle
with Ms. Dracaena!

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:26.710
I thought you might say that!

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:27.840
Then...

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:30.630
The time has come for science
to usher in our future!

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.090
Citronic Gear, on!

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:43.350
I imagined something like this could happen
and prepared this nice machine!

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.730
I call it the Pokémotion Capture!

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:47.280
Ooh!

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:49.490
Another lame name.

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.490
Eureka!

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:53.950
Huh? Go?

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.410
Yeah! I was surprised to hear
you know one another!

00:09:57.870 --> 00:10:00.960
She gave me some advice
when I was trying to catch this!

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:07.590
Ooh, a Keromatsu? Good job!

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:08.210
Yeah!

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:10.010
Nice to meet you!

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.590
I’m the Miare Gym Leader, Citron.

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.970
Hi. My name is Go.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.390
I hear you’re an incredible inventor.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:19.520
Oh, no, far from it.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:24.100
I just hope to invent things
that can make people and Pokémon happy.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:25.810
Then you made this robot, too?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:26.730
Yes.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:28.690
I am Citroid. Nice to meet you.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:30.530
Amazing!

00:10:30.530 --> 00:10:32.900
Here, take this.
I got you some souvenirs.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:33.990
They’re Miare Galettes!

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:36.740
Oh! Thank you!

00:10:36.740 --> 00:10:38.370
Let’s eat them together later!

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.500
Oh, that sounds good.

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:43.620
It’s so cute!

00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:47.840
Tickle-tickle-tickle-tickle!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.260
Is this one of Satoshi’s Pokémon?

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.970
Yeah. It’s called Uonoragon.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:56.260
It’s apparently a very rare Pokémon
from the Galar Region!

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:59.350
I’m Eureka!
Nice to meet you!

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.020
Tickle-tickle-tickle-tickle!

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:04.270
Satoshi! Let’s get started.

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:04.270
So cute!

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:05.770
All right!

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:08.190
Negigaknight! Let’s do it!

00:11:13.240 --> 00:11:15.740
Well then, Pokémotion Capture...

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:17.700
Let’s get capping!

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.370
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:50.940 --> 00:11:51.900
I see...

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:54.280
I’m beginning to see the problem.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:55.280
Ooh...

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:59.700
Star Assault involves gathering the energy
given off by his body into his chest.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.780
It takes time to charge.

00:12:01.780 --> 00:12:03.700
That’s step one.

00:12:03.700 --> 00:12:04.790
Mhm, mhm.

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:10.790
Step two is sending that charged energy into his sword,
and then thrusting it forward.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.460
<i>Ahh...</i>

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:13.300
How come?

00:12:13.300 --> 00:12:16.220
Good question.
Which brings us to the third step.

00:12:16.220 --> 00:12:21.180
Normally, he would hit the enemy
with that energy stored in the tip,

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:27.270
but for Satoshi’s Negigaknight, the core of his body
wobbles in the transfer from charge to thrust.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:30.940
The tip of the sword fails to stabilize,
and the focused energy falls apart.

00:12:30.940 --> 00:12:34.980
Eliminating that wobble will be
the key to perfecting the move.

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:36.530
Ooh!

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:39.950
And this is what I’ve simulated.

00:12:39.950 --> 00:12:42.620
Stillness into motion,
motion into stillness.

00:12:42.620 --> 00:12:45.250
If you can pull that off fluidly,
and stably,

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:48.580
Star Assault is sure to exhibit
incredible strength.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:52.590
The power of science is amazing!

00:12:52.590 --> 00:12:54.340
But why does he wobble?

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:58.550
Looking at the data,
compared to when he was a Kamonegi...

00:12:58.550 --> 00:13:01.430
Between his sword and shield,
he’s carrying far more weight now.

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:07.270
I believe that extra weight
is what’s making his body sway.

00:13:07.270 --> 00:13:12.150
But just before, it was strong enough to
blow away Uonoragon...

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:19.780
I think that being bitten by Uonoragon
stabilized Negigaknight’s stance

00:13:19.780 --> 00:13:22.160
and let him concentrate
on the move.

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:25.370
Uonoragon, you’re amazing!

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:27.290
Thank you, Uonoragon.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.580
If only there was some way
he could control the charge and thrust...

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:36.090
Okay, Negigaknight!
Train with me!

00:13:37.340 --> 00:13:38.630
Citroid!

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.470
Lemme borrow these flags!

00:13:41.470 --> 00:13:42.840
Understood.

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.220
What now?
What’s he gonna do?

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:47.430
Listen up, Negigaknight.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:51.060
Focus your feelings here,
then thrust them toward your opponent!

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.350
One...

00:13:53.350 --> 00:13:54.190
Two...

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.110
Three!

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:59.610
This “snap” is
the most important part!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.740
If you can do that,
your sword won’t wobble!

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.910
One... Two... Three!

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:13.460
One... Two... Three!

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:18.380
One... Two... Three!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.760
One... Two... Three!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.930
That’s a very Satoshi
way of teaching.

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:24.720
Yeah.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.470
They’ve trained together
ever since he was a Kamonegi.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:29.890
I know they’ll be able to
pull it off next time!

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.810
You know... When I’m battling...

00:14:32.810 --> 00:14:35.190
If I’m watching my opponent...

00:14:35.190 --> 00:14:37.520
I go “vwoosh” and focus in on them!

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:42.530
Times like that...
I don’t even notice anything else around me!

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:46.240
Yeah, Satoshi really is incredible
when he’s focused.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.200
Indeed!

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:50.290
So I bet... If you...

00:14:50.290 --> 00:14:52.540
...keep focusing on
your opponent, too...

00:14:52.540 --> 00:14:55.790
Your sword and shield
will feel like they weigh nothing!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.420
Know what I mean?

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:03.050
Ack!

00:15:14.190 --> 00:15:15.690
This again!

00:15:18.190 --> 00:15:19.440
What? What?

00:15:33.830 --> 00:15:35.290
What happened...?

00:15:35.290 --> 00:15:38.210
Oh, this always happens...

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:46.050
It looks happy!

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:47.970
I thought so!

00:15:47.970 --> 00:15:52.890
Being bitten by Uonoragon stabilized the sword
and let him concentrate on the move!

00:15:52.890 --> 00:15:58.400
Oh, so that means Uonoragon is like
training wheels on a bike!

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.770
They help you ride
when you’re starting out.

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:05.070
But once you get the hang of it,
you can keep your balance just fine without them!

00:16:05.070 --> 00:16:07.030
That’s a good example, Go!

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:09.530
Y-You think so?

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.490
So that’s it!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.790
Negigaknight!

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:17.790
Your focus got a lot better
because of Uonoragon!

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:21.090
Focus on the opponent in front of you!
You’re gonna win!

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:25.170
Those feelings are gonna help you
perfect your Star Assault!

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:32.140
Yeah.

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:34.890
Battle problems will have
battle solutions.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.850
How about a practice battle
with me?

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.360
All right!
Let’s make it a double battle!

00:16:40.360 --> 00:16:42.360
Huh? A double battle?

00:16:42.360 --> 00:16:46.110
Yeah! Uonoragon’s speed
when biting the sword...

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.030
Its power to withstand
Negigaknight’s attacks...

00:16:49.030 --> 00:16:50.530
I wanna try ‘em out!

00:16:52.200 --> 00:16:55.160
Ms. Dracaena is a Dragon-user.

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.210
I can see why you'd want to fight her
with a Dragon type.

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.460
Got it!

00:16:59.460 --> 00:17:02.790
In that case... Rentorar! Horudo!

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.130
Please lend me a hand!

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:10.090
Commencing practice battle
between Satoshi and Citron!

00:17:14.890 --> 00:17:18.020
Rentorar!
Use Wild Bolt on Negigaknight!

00:17:18.020 --> 00:17:20.730
Horudo,
Dig towards Uonoragon!

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:26.780
Negigaknight!
Use Star Assault on Rentorar!

00:17:26.780 --> 00:17:29.490
Uonoragon,
you use Jaw Bite on Horudo!

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:45.210
Uonoragon! Wait, wait!

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:51.970
Uonoragon!

00:17:56.890 --> 00:18:00.100
So I bet if you keep focusing on
your opponent, too...

00:18:00.100 --> 00:18:03.980
Your sword and shield
will feel like they weigh nothing!

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:10.570
He stopped wobbling!

00:18:10.570 --> 00:18:12.110
Go!

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.130
A perfect Star Assault!

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:33.130
The training wheels are off!

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.640
Uonoragon looks happy, too!

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:38.390
You finally did it,
Negigaknight!

00:18:43.060 --> 00:18:45.270
He can’t move from the recoil?

00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:56.280
What now?

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.700
Its power is rising...

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:00.120
Uonoragon...

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.870
Horudo!
Use Arm Hammer on Uonoragon!

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.650
The practice battle is concluded!

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:38.160
Thank you, Citron.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:40.910
I’m glad I could be of help.

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:43.870
That looked like
Dragon Dive just now!

00:19:43.870 --> 00:19:45.460
Dragon Dive?

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:50.130
Maybe it tried to copy Star Assault
but it turned into a Dragon Dive!

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:51.340
Huh?

00:19:51.340 --> 00:19:53.010
That can happen?!

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.430
I get it...

00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:58.470
You got a power-up too, Uonoragon!

00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.580
Huh?

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.120
They look like they get along.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.250
At this rate,
tomorrow’s battle...

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.670
...is looking promising!

00:20:31.670 --> 00:20:32.380
Yeah!

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.500
All right!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:37.630
Negigaknight! Uonoragon!
I’m picking you two tomorrow!

00:20:38.180 --> 00:20:40.350
Negigaknight and Uonoragon...

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:42.600
An unexpected tag team.

00:20:43.140 --> 00:20:48.060
And Satoshi finally heads to challenge
Dracaena of the Kalos Elite Four!

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:51.770
Chevargo!
Use Consecutive Cut!

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.230
Wide Breaker!

00:20:58.740 --> 00:21:01.490
You are as sharp as I thought,
Mr. Gampi.

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:05.370
I would say the same for thee!
I cannot relax for a moment!

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:09.290
I have you! Finishing Stinger!

00:21:11.290 --> 00:21:13.340
Heat Wave!

00:21:22.010 --> 00:21:23.140
Marvelous!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:26.310
Your sharp moves are captivating!

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:29.140
Tyltalis and thou
truly move together as one!

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.110
Thank you.

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:37.940
Let’s show Competitor Satoshi
just how strong the Kalos Elite Four are.

00:23:07.160 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.410 --> 00:23:12.910
We finally get to battle!

00:23:12.910 --> 00:23:15.380
Dracaena of the Elite Four!

00:23:15.380 --> 00:23:18.170
Negigaknight and Uonoragon...
Go for it!

00:23:18.170 --> 00:23:20.880
I had a look at your battle record.

00:23:20.880 --> 00:23:21.800
However...

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:25.760
Your forward march ends today.

00:23:25.760 --> 00:23:27.510
It’s your turn, Tyltalis!

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:30.680
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:34.190
Hyper Class!
VS Elite Four Dracaena!!
